Nature Reviews Microbiology

(2026) Cite this article









            Save article




                View saved research

Subjects

            Climate changeFungal ecologyFungal evolutionFungal infectionFungal pathogenesis

As climate variability intensifies, human-pathogenic fungi are spreading into new regions and causing more disease. Addressing emergence will require stronger surveillance and forecasting; research on fungal dispersal, adaptation and population immunity; and policies that support vaccine development, antifungal stewardship and diagnostic access.

